      "summary": "The redaction filter does not meet the required JWT recognition behavior for headers with leading JSON whitespace, and the added tests do not exercise that case.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/RedactionFilter.cs",
          "line": 22,
          "message": "JWTs with leading JSON whitespace in the encoded header bypass redaction (OWASP A09:2025).",
          "confidence": 0.98,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Log properties, scopes, and trace attributes pass through ScrubText, which uses Jwt() to recognize JWT-shaped values. The regex only accepts headers whose base64url encoding starts with ew or ey; it does not decode the header and validate it as JSON.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs a valid compact JWT whose JSON header has leading whitespace, such as a header encoding beginning IHsi. Jwt() does not match it, so the token can reach a log provider or trace exporter unredacted, contrary to acceptance criterion 2 (OWASP A09:2025). The current tests use headers with whitespace after the opening brace, so they do not cover this case."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
