      "summary": "The exporter registration tests and the logging and trace redaction tests cover the other stated behaviors. The JWT matcher and its regression test do not cover the explicitly required whitespace-prefixed header.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/RedactionFilter.cs",
          "line": 22,
          "message": "JWT redaction misses valid tokens with leading JSON whitespace in the encoded header, contrary to acceptance criterion 2.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "ScrubText applies Jwt() to log values and trace attributes. The regex only matches JWT headers beginning with `ey` or `ew`; it does not decode the base64url header or validate it as JSON.",
            "failureScenario": "A valid JWT with a leading space in its JSON header has a base64url header beginning `IH` (for example, `IHsiYWxnIjoiSFMyNTYifQ.e30.c2ln`). Logged under an ordinary property name, it does not match Jwt() and reaches the provider unchanged. The regression test uses `ey Ai...`, which does not encode a leading space, so it passes without verifying the required case. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
